<BaseLayout title="Vanderbilt Bellydance (Archived)" description="Archived Vanderbilt Dance Program bellydance class listing.">
	<h1>Vanderbilt Dance Program</h1>
	<p class="lede">Belly Dance Class</p>
	<p><em>Archived listing from Reischa's time as a Vanderbilt Dance Program instructor.</em></p>

	<div class="class-info-grid">
		<div>
			<h2>Beginner / Intermediate Bellydance</h2>
			<p>Class started August 25th, 2014. Mondays, 6:00 &ndash; 7:00 PM.</p>
			<p>
				Beginner / Intermediate Level, Studio A. This is an
				introduction to the fundamentals of belly dance used in all
				styles. Fundamentals will be covered through a series of
				basic technique exercises, combinations, and choreography.
				This is a beginner level class, but it is also a wonderful
				refresher course. This class will include Intermediate level
				information.
			</p>

			<h2>Intermediate / Advanced Bellydance</h2>
			<p>
				This class is not meeting until further notice. For the time
				being, the Intermediate Class is being integrated into the
				Beginner Class listed above.
			</p>
			<p>
				This is a continuation of belly dance fundamentals.
				Challenging exercises, combinations, choreography, and even
				improvisation will be studied.
				<strong>This is an intermediate level class recommended to students with prior study.</strong>
			</p>

			<p>
				Feel free to email / call Reischa with questions regarding
				these classes.<br />
				<a href="mailto:luri7@yahoo.com">luri7@yahoo.com</a><br />
				615-593-7119
			</p>
		</div>

		<dl class="class-meta">
			<dt>Class Meeting Location</dt>
			<dd>Memorial Gym<br />2201 West End<br />Nashville, TN 37240</dd>

			<dt>Registration Dates</dt>
			<dd>
				Aug 19th &ndash; 23rd at Sarratt Center Lobby.
				(<a href="http://www.vanderbilt.edu/dance/about-the-program/directions/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Directions</a>)<br />
				12&ndash;6 PM Tuesday&ndash;Friday / 11am&ndash;4pm Saturday, <strong>OR</strong> late registration at the Memorial Gym Dance Studios (cash or check only).
			</dd>

			<dt>Pricing</dt>
			<dd>
				14-week session.<br />
				Community Members / Non-students: $136<br />
				VU Faculty / Staff: $124<br />
				VU Students: $112<br />
				Single Classes: $12.00 each
			</dd>

			<dt>Contact Information</dt>
			<dd>
				Please contact Kelvin Amburgy at the Vanderbilt Dance Program
				for more registration information.<br />
				Sarratt Center: 322-2471 / 322-6400<br />
				<a href="http://www.vanderbilt.edu/dance" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Website</a>
			</dd>
		</dl>
	</div>

	<a class="back-link" href="/classes/">&larr; Back to Classes</a>
